---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import {
  AvatarPlayground,
  AvatarSizes,
  AgentAvatarSizes,
  EntityAvatars,
  AvatarGroups,
  AgentCompositions,
  EntityCompositions,
  ChatCompositions,
} from '../../components/AvatarDemo';
---

<Docs title="Avatar">
  <h1 class="docs-title">Avatar</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    Pictures for people, agents, and workspaces. Shows initials when there is no image or the image fails. Built with
    Base UI.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <AvatarPlayground client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Avatar usage"
      code={`import {
  Avatar, AvatarImage, AvatarFallback, AvatarBadge,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/avatar";

<Avatar size="lg">
  <AvatarImage src={user.image} alt={user.name} />
  <AvatarFallback>AM</AvatarFallback>
  <AvatarBadge role="img" aria-label="Verified">
    <CheckIcon aria-hidden="true" />
  </AvatarBadge>
</Avatar>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>Avatar</code> takes <code>size</code>: <code>"xs"</code>, <code>"sm"</code>, <code>"default"</code>, or{' '}
      <code>"lg"</code>. The fallback shows while the image loads, when it fails, and when there is no image. Use
      <code>delay</code> on <code>AvatarFallback</code> to avoid a flash on fast networks. The image fades in over
      180ms; reduced motion turns this off.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4">
      <AvatarSizes client:load />
      <AvatarGroups client:load />
    </div>
    <p>
      <code>AvatarBadge</code> sits on the bottom edge. Its icon hides at small sizes.
      <code>AvatarGroup</code> overlaps avatars, and <code>AvatarGroupCount</code> matches their size. Set{' '}
      <code>--sprout-avatar-ring</code> to the surface color behind a group or badge.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Agent avatars</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Agent avatar"
      code={`<AgentAvatar agentId={agent.id} name={agent.name} size="sm" />`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>AgentAvatar</code> picks stable artwork from <code>agentId</code>. The image is decorative; put the agent
      name in nearby text. Pass <code>src</code> to use your own artwork. <code>agentAvatarSrc(id, baseUrl)</code>{' '}
      returns the default URL.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6">
      <AgentAvatarSizes client:load />
    </div>
    <AgentCompositions client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Entity avatars</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Entity avatar"
      code={`<EntityAvatar
  seed={workspace.id}
  name={workspace.name}
  image={workspace.icon}
  size="xs"
  shape="square"
/>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>EntityAvatar</code> takes a <code>seed</code>, <code>name</code>, optional <code>image</code>,{' '}
      <code>size</code> up to <code>"xl"</code>, and <code>shape</code> (<code>"circle"</code> or <code>"square"</code>
      ). Without an image it shows the first letter on a gradient. The same seed always gives the same gradient. An
      empty name shows <code>?</code>.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6">
      <EntityAvatars client:load />
    </div>
    <EntityCompositions client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">In conversations</h2>
    <ChatCompositions client:load />
    <p>
      Image upload, file checks, menus, tables, and messages above are sample code. The package only draws the avatar.
      Your application owns data, uploads, and navigation.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      Give <code>AvatarImage</code> real <code>alt</code> text when the avatar is the only name on screen. Use{' '}
      <code>alt=""</code> when a name is next to it. Avatars are not focusable; put them inside a link or button for
      actions. Give badges and icon counts an accessible label.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
